    <statement><p>Use the product rule to differentiate.</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle \frac{d}{dx} ( e^{2x} ) =  \frac{d}{dx} ( e^x \cdot e^{x} ) =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/> .</p>
<p>Now use the product rule again to differentiate.</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle \frac{d}{dx} ( e^{3x} ) =  \frac{d}{dx} ( e^x \cdot e^{2x} ) =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0002"/> .</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>2\exp\mathopen{}\left(2x\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>3\exp\mathopen{}\left(3x\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
